Spec: PublisherRuntimes

Purpose:
  Publish approved local exports through the authenticated backend without static profiles.

Owns:
  ./PublisherRuntimes.cs

References:
  ./FrpRuntimeBridge.sdd

Must:
  Use a fifteen-second transport heartbeat response timeout while retaining one-second emission and independent authority invalidation.
  Retry failed startup with per-application bounded exponential backoff, retain capacity for failed cleanup and close publishers on authority-storage failure.
  Discover only explicitly approved publisher applications, with at most sixteen owned publishers and fixed local inner-mTLS targets.
  Derive STCP/XTCP proxies from approved service IDs, current review generations and explicit server/STUN settings; never create authority from registration.
  Retire revoked, changed or dead publishers and clean only owned processes/files; preserve existing publishers across denial-only reviews.
  Report local process presence separately from remote registration/business readiness.
